{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014DN8CgwE6YvBcwMsx5Z41E","type":"tool_result","content":"test(01): sample fractional and far start times, record acceptance\n\n .planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-VALIDATION.md | 4 ++++\n tests/test_budget.py                              | 2 ++\n 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+)\ncommit 7d8b545d43890a52ac72bde17c22dc49ebaca1a5\nAuthor: DevFlow Probe <devflow-probe@localhost>\nDate:   Mon Nov 2 14:24:08 2026 -0500\n\n    test(01): sample fractional and far start times, record acceptance\n\ndiff --git a/tests/test_budget.py b/tests/test_budget.py\nindex 2d40fb8..249ef89 100644\n--- a/tests/test_budget.py\n+++ b/tests/test_budget.py\n@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@ class RetryBudgetTest(unittest.TestCase):\n         self.assertEqual(deadline_after(10.0), 10.0 + DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS)\n         self.assertEqual(deadline_after(0.0), DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS)\n         self.assertEqual(deadline_after(-5.0), -5.0 + DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS)\n+        for start in (1.5, -5.25, 1800000000.25, -1000.0):\n+            self.assertEqual(deadline_after(start), start + DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS)\n \n \n if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n---\nphase: 01-retry-budget\nreviewed: 2026-11-02T00:00:00Z\ndepth: standard\nfiles_reviewed: 1\nfiles_reviewed_list:\n  - tests/test_budget.py\nfindings:\n  critical: 0\n  warning: 2\n  info: 2\n  total: 4\nstatus: issues_found\n---\n\n# Phase 01: Code Review Report\n\n**Reviewed:** 2026-11-02\n**Depth:** standard\n**Files Reviewed:** 1\n**Status:** issues_found\n\n## Summary\n\nReviewed `tests/test_budget.py` with `probe/budget.py` as context. Both tests pass (`Ran 2 tests ... OK`). I also ran mutations in a scratch copy under `$HOME/.cache` (since removed): budget set to 30, 300 and 150 each failed the first test. A literal `120` in `deadline_after` with the constant at 121 failed both tests. A literal `120` with the constant at 120 passed.\n\nWhat that establishes: the tests catch a wrong budget value and a wrong deadline formula. What it does not establish: that the budget value is correct (the 120 choice is unconfirmed by a human, per the disposition file), or any behavior of non-finite or non-float input.\n\nNo security issues or crashes. The defects are in the test design.\n\n## Warnings\n\n### WR-03: Budget test is self-contradictory and collapses to `== 120`\n\n**File:** `tests/test_budget.py:5,11-13`\n**Issue:** `OFFERED_BUDGETS = (30, 120, 300)` is asserted as the acceptable set. The range assertions then require `90 < value < 240`, which excludes 30 and 300. The intersection of the two is `{120}`, so the test is equivalent to `assertEqual(..., 120)` spelled as three assertions. Verified by mutation: 30 fails on `30 not greater than 90`, 300 fails on `300 not less than 240`, and 150 fails on `not found in (30, 120, 300)`.\n\nThis conflicts with `01-REVIEW-DISPOSITION.md` (WR-01), which says an operator \"can override it by changing `probe/budget.py`\". Overriding to any other offered value (30 or 300) turns the suite red, so the override needs a test edit too. The test name says \"one of the offered values\" but it enforces one specific value.\n\n**Fix:** Decide what the test is meant to pin. Either pin the chosen value explicitly:\n```python\nCHOSEN_BUDGET_SECS = 120\nself.assertEqual(DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, CHOSEN_BUDGET_SECS)\n```\nor, if the contract is \"an offered value that satisfies the failover and pager constraints\", name the constraints and filter the offers by them:\n```python\nUPSTREAM_FAILOVER_SECS = 90\nPAGER_ESCALATION_SECS = 240\nself.assertIn(DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, OFFERED_BUDGETS)\nself.assertGreater(DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, UPSTREAM_FAILOVER_SECS)\nself.assertLess(DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, PAGER_ESCALATION_SECS)\n```\nand drop or justify offered values the range can never accept.\n\n### WR-04: Deadline test restates the implementation and cannot tell the constant from a literal\n\n**File:** `tests/test_budget.py:16-18`\n**Issue:** All three assertions compute the expected value as `start + DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS`, which is the implementation's own expression. The test shows `deadline_after` adds the constant. It does not show that it adds the constant rather than a hardcoded number: a literal `120` in `deadline_after` passes whenever the constant is also 120 (verified). The test also never checks an independent expected number, so its result depends on `DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` being right, which is the other test's job. Three inputs (10.0, 0.0, -5.0) all exercise the same single code path.\n\n**Fix:** Patch the constant so the test is independent of its real value:\n```python\nfrom unittest import mock\n\nwith mock.patch(\"probe.budget.DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS\", 7):\n    self.assertEqual(deadline_after(10.0), 17.0)\n```\nThat fails if the function uses a literal or a stale copy of the budget.\n\n## Info\n\n### IN-03: Magic numbers 90 and 240 duplicate a comment in the source module\n\n**File:** `tests/test_budget.py:12-13`\n**Issue:** The bounds come from the comment in `probe/budget.py:3-4` (90-second failover, 240-second pager escalation). The comment's figures cannot be checked from this repo (see disposition IN-01). The test copies them as bare literals, so the source and the test can drift without any link between them.\n**Fix:** Name the constants as in WR-03, or export them from `probe/budget.py` and import them in the test.\n\n### IN-04: `assertIsInstance(..., int)` does not exclude `bool`, and no test covers input type or non-finite input\n\n**File:** `tests/test_budget.py:10,15-18`\n**Issue:** `bool` is a subclass of `int`, so the isinstance check is weaker than it looks. Here the `assertIn` that follows makes it harmless, because `True` is not in the offered set. `deadline_after` is untested for `int` input (returns `int`, not `float`), `nan` and `inf`. The disposition file defers this because no caller exists yet. I agree it is latent, not a defect today.\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 1 test in 0.000s\n\nFAILED (errors=1)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XzTeX8F74zjvGz97A8AxLk","agent_id":"a984cb6695fdc67f6","session_id":"uuid-10","uuid":"uuid-1089","timestamp":"2026-11-02T19:26:40.393Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014DN8CgwE6YvBcwMsx5Z41E","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"gsd-code-reviewer","task_description":"Review phase 01 test change"}
